The decidable version replaces $\mathrm{Prop}$ with $\mathrm{Bool}$ and $
eg$ with boolean negation $!$. The key lemma `bnot_has_no_fixpoint` is proved by `cases b <;> decide` — Lean's kernel computation verifies $!\mathrm{true} 
eq \mathrm{true}$ and $!\mathrm{false} 
eq \mathrm{false}$ automatically. This variant is useful in computational contexts where classical propositions are unavailable.
